  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – catching in pairs",
  "description": "The keepers work in two pairs. A and C serve the ball to B and D, who each stand in a small cone goal. B and D catch it and roll it back. After a few balls everyone swaps places diagonally: A takes D's place and D takes A's, and B and C do the same.\n\nMake it harder step by step: 1) low balls played with the foot, 2) thrown balls at stomach height, 3) thrown balls at the face. Rotate so both pairs get to work in the big goal. Works with 2–5 keepers.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Ready position: knees slightly bent, weight on the front of the feet and hands in front of the body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Thumbs and index fingers behind the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Take the ball in front of you and watch it all the way into your hands."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
